Save a local Docker image and publish it through the authenticated platform registry API. This is an ergonomic alias for `registry push` and supports tenant, org, and public scopes.

Usage:
  mcp-runtime server push [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help           help for push
      --image string   Local image to push (required)
      --name string    Override target repository/name
      --scope string   Publish scope: tenant, org, or public

Global Flags:
      --debug      Enable debug mode with structured error logging
      --use-kube   Use direct Kubernetes mode with kubectl; requires admin/operator cluster access (admin/dev/test only)
